# 5. Resource & Effort Estimate
- 1 QA Automation Engineer (API/Backend) – 2 weeks
- 1 Security Tester – 1 week
- 1 Performance Engineer – 1 week
- Total Duration: 3 weeks (parallelizable)

# 6. Test Schedule / Milestone
- Week 1: Test environment setup, credential matrix prep, negative/positive API auth test scripts
- Week 2: Security/permission boundary tests, error handling validation, performance/SLA simulation
- Week 3: Results review, defect triage, regression, and final reporting

# 7. Assumptions
- Test credentials and environments are available and stable
- Mock Jira API service can be configured for all required auth states
- Tooling access (Playwright, PyTest, JMeter, OWASP ZAP, tcconfig) is provisioned

# 8. Dependencies
- Jira API endpoint availability
- Test credential provisioning
- Mock service deployment

# 9. Risk Mitigation Table
| Risk ID | Description | Impact | Probability | Severity | Mitigation Action | Owner |
|---------|-------------|--------|-------------|----------|-------------------|-------|
| R1      | Dynamic Jira API endpoint instability | High   | Medium      | High     | Use mock service fallback for endpoint outages | QA Lead |
| R2      | Test credential provisioning delays   | Medium | Medium      | Medium   | Request credentials in advance, escalate to IT | QA Lead |
| R3      | Tool access/configuration issues      | Medium | Low         | Medium   | Pre-validate tool access, maintain backup scripts | QA Lead |
| R4      | SLA/latency test environment not available | Medium | Low    | Medium   | Simulate with tcconfig, coordinate with infra team | Perf Eng |
| R5      | Reviewer timeout during validation loop | Medium | Medium | Medium | Implement reviewer reminders, auto-escalate after 24h | QA Lead |

